---
import Base from '../../../../layouts/Base.astro';

const SITE = 'https://precisionsolutionstech.com';
const title = 'Flipside for Android Privacy Policy | Precision Solutions Tech';
const description =
  'How Flipside for Android handles your camera, photos, microphone and motion. Everything runs on your device; the app has no internet permission and collects nothing.';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${SITE}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Privacy Policy', item: `${SITE}/legal/privacy/` },
      {
        '@type': 'ListItem',
        position: 3,
        name: 'Flipside for Android',
        item: `${SITE}/legal/privacy/flipside-android/`,
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'Flipside for Android Privacy Policy',
    url: `${SITE}/legal/privacy/flipside-android/`,
    description,
    dateModified: '2026-11-01',
    isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', name: 'Precision Solutions Tech', url: `${SITE}/` },
  },
];
---

<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/legal/privacy/flipside-android/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
        <li><a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a></li>
        <li>Flipside for Android</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <article class="prose">
      <h1>Flipside for Android Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="meta">Last updated: November 1, 2026</p>
      <p class="lead">
        This Privacy Policy describes how <strong>Flipside</strong> (“we”, “us”) handles information
        when you use the Flipside app for Android (the “App”), published by
        <strong>Precision Solutions Tech</strong>, operated by <strong>SG TECHNOLOGY LLC</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="summary">Short version</h2>
      <p>
        Flipside works <strong>entirely on your device</strong>. Your camera, your photos, your voice
        and everything the App measures stay on your phone. We collect no data, operate no account
        system, and run no servers that receive anything from the App. The App does not have
        Android’s internet permission, so it cannot send anything over the network, and it never asks
        for your location.
      </p>

      <h2 id="camera">Camera</h2>
      <p>
        The App uses the camera to coach you into the shot: it finds faces, people, hands (for the
        raised-palm shutter) and pets, and measures framing and light in the live picture, on your
        device. Live frames are analysed and discarded; they are not stored or sent anywhere. For jump
        shots the App keeps the last few seconds of the live picture in memory so it can pick the
        frames where you are in the air; the rest are thrown away. Only the photos you take are kept,
        and only while you use them in the App, until you save or share them.
      </p>

      <h2 id="microphone">Microphone and speech recognition (optional)</h2>
      <p>
        Only if you turn on “Say cheese”, the App asks for the microphone and listens for words like
        “cheese” or “take it” while the camera screen is open. Recognition uses
        <strong>Android’s on-device speech recognizer only</strong> (Android 13 and later). If your
        phone has no on-device recognizer, the App tells you “Say cheese” is unavailable rather than
        using an online service, so your voice is never sent to Google or to us. Nothing is recorded
        or kept.
      </p>

      <h2 id="motion">Motion</h2>
      <p>
        The App reads the motion sensors while the camera is open, to tell a phone in your hand from
        one on a stand, to keep scenic shots level, and to take the photo at the steadiest moment.
        These readings are used on the spot and not stored.
      </p>

      <h2 id="photos">Photos and videos</h2>
      <p>
        When you save, the App adds the photo to your phone’s Pictures folder (and a jump loop video
        to Movies), in a Flipside folder. This needs no storage permission, and the App does not read
        the rest of your gallery. The App has no location permission, so saved and shared photos carry
        no location information.
      </p>

      <h2 id="learning">What the App learns about your phone</h2>
      <p>
        Android phones differ in how long the camera takes to fire and how long the voice takes to
        start, so the App measures these on your phone and remembers them, along with how soon after
        “Jump!” people tend to jump. What it keeps is a short list of timings in seconds, such as
        “this camera fires 0.5 seconds after it is asked”. It contains no pictures and nothing about who
        you are. It is stored in the App’s private storage, is left out of device backups, and is
        removed when you clear the App’s storage or uninstall it.
      </p>

      <h2 id="processing">What the App processes on your device</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Faces, bodies, hands and pets, head pose and eye openness, to coach, choose the best photo and fix blinks</li>
        <li>A person outline, for background blur and jump combos</li>
        <li>Scene type and light, to choose camera settings</li>
        <li>The camera and voice timings described above</li>
        <li>Your settings: voice output, timer, shooting style, hands-free options</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This uses Google’s ML Kit and MediaPipe models, which are built into the App and run on your
        phone; because the App has no internet permission, they cannot send anything either. None of
        this is used to identify you, and none of it leaves your device. Spoken directions use your
        phone’s own text-to-speech.
      </p>

      <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
      <p>
        The App is not directed to children under 13 (or the minimum age in your jurisdiction) and
        asks no one for personal information. Photos of anyone, of any age, are handled the same way:
        on your device, never collected by us.
      </p>

      <h2 id="sharing">Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        When you share a photo or video, Android’s share sheet sends it to the app you choose
        (Messages, email, social apps), and that service’s own privacy policy applies.
      </p>

      <h2 id="analytics">Analytics, tracking, and advertising</h2>
      <p>
        The App contains <strong>no analytics SDKs, no advertising SDKs, and no third-party
        trackers</strong>. We do not profile you, and we do not sell or share personal information. If
        that ever changes, this policy will be updated before the change ships.
      </p>

      <h2 id="retention">Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        We hold no data from the App. Photos you save are yours to keep or delete. Your settings and the
        timings the App has learned stay on your phone until you clear the App’s storage or uninstall
        it. If you contact support, we keep your message as long as needed to help you.
      </p>

      <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy. The “Last updated” date will change when we do.</p>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions:
        <a href="mailto:support@precisionsolutionstech.com">support@precisionsolutionstech.com</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/legal/privacy/flipside-ios/">Flipside for iPhone privacy policy</a>
        ·
        <a href="/legal/privacy/">Company privacy policy</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
